>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_codatatype`

``` hol4
Refute.register_codatatype :
  {tyop : {Thy : string, Tyop : string},
   case_const : term,
   constructors : term list,
   witness : thm option} -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Registers an existing codatatype with the model finder.

`tyop` names the type operator, whose parameters must be distinct type
variables.  `constructors` lists its distinct constructor constants in
cases-theorem order; each must have a `tyop`-headed result type at its
own declared type, not merely at the instance supplied (so `combin$I`,
whose declared result is a type variable, is rejected).  `case_const`
is the case constant; its scrutinee position is inferred and must be
unique, in any argument, and the remaining arguments are checked against
the constructor branches.

Shape alone cannot separate a codatatype from an inductive datatype, so
the constructor list is otherwise the caller's assertion, checked two
ways.  When the datatype database already knows `tyop` as a free
datatype, every constructor must be one of its database constructors by
key, which rejects an impostor constant declared at the right type.
`witness = SOME thm` rules out generic shape defeats: after stripping
outer `!`s, `thm`'s conclusion must be `?x. body`, `body` an equation
in either orientation between `x` and a constructor application
`C a1 ... an`, where `C`'s key matches a registered constructor and `x`
is `aconv` to an argument reached by walking the constructor spine,
descending only through arguments whose head is again a registered
constructor.  `C` need not be fully applied, so `x`'s type need not be
`tyop`-headed or the generic instance.  HOL4's per-type bisimulation
theorems and mutual-cycle witnesses are not of this shape; a caller
holding one passes `witness = NONE`, which registers on trust.  A wrong
registration removes the type's acyclicity constraints and can produce
a wrong model.

Registrations are session-local.  Built-in lazy registrations cover
`llist`, `ltree`, `itree`, `itreeTau`, `lbtree`, and `path` when their
theories are loaded; they go through the same shape check directly, so
no witness applies to them.

### Failure

Fails for an empty or duplicate constructor list, nonconstant terms,
wrong constructor results or case branches, an ambiguous or absent
scrutinee position, interpreted or function types, malformed type
parameters, a witness of the wrong shape, or an incompatible quotient,
typedef, or fraction classification.

### See also

[`Refute.register_quotient`](#Refute.register_quotient),
[`Refute.register_typedef`](#Refute.register_typedef),
[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Codatatype bounds are described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
